@startuml dataflow_review_publish_pipeline
!theme plain
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam SequenceArrowThickness 1.5

title Data Flow: Review and Publish Pipeline\n(Human-in-the-loop -> Outbox -> Graph Sync)

actor "Instructor" as Instructor
participant "web-bff\nReview Inbox" as Web
participant "core-api" as Core
database "PostgreSQL\ncards + quiz + outbox" as PG
queue "Redis\nBullMQ" as Redis
participant "Outbox Poller" as Outbox
participant "graph-sync worker" as GraphWorker
database "Neo4j\nKnowledge Graph" as Neo4j

== 1. Review drafts ==
Instructor -> Web : open Review Inbox
Web -> Core : GET /review-items\nstatus=GENERATED_DRAFT
Core -> PG : SELECT lesson_cards,\nquiz_items
PG --> Core : drafts[]
Core --> Web : drafts with citations
Web --> Instructor : show card / quiz\nwith source references

== 2. Edit and approve ==
Instructor -> Web : Edit / Approve / Reject
Web -> Core : PATCH /review-items/{id}\ncontent + decision
Core -> PG : UPDATE status\nREVIEWING / APPROVED /\nCHANGES_REQUESTED
Core --> Web : saved

== 3. Atomic publish transaction ==
Instructor -> Web : Publish
Web -> Core : POST /review-items/{id}/publish
Core -> PG : BEGIN\nUPDATE item status=PUBLISHED\nINSERT outbox_events\nCOMMIT
Core --> Web : {status=PUBLISHED}

note right of PG
  Business update and outbox event
  share the same transaction to
  avoid split-brain between PostgreSQL
  and downstream stores.
end note

== 4. Async graph projection ==
Outbox -> PG : SELECT outbox_events\nWHERE status=PENDING
Outbox -> Redis : enqueue GraphProjectionRequested
GraphWorker -> Redis : consume GraphProjectionRequested
GraphWorker -> PG : LOAD published item + LO mappings
GraphWorker -> Neo4j : MERGE Card / QuizItem\nMERGE relations\n[:GROUNDED_IN] / [:ASSESSES]
GraphWorker -> PG : UPDATE outbox_events status=PROCESSED

== 5. Serving to learners ==
Web -> Core : GET /published-content
Core -> PG : SELECT PUBLISHED items
Core --> Web : card / quiz ready for learners

@enduml
